    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="4.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 4.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="310" ed="#liebermann"/>And we beodað, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wiðersacan ⁊ utlagan Godes ⁊ manna of eardæ<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IICn_4-1.lnote.oe.21"/> gewitan, butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IICn_4-1.lnote.oe.22"/> hig gebugan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#IICn_4-1.lnote.oe.23"/> ⁊ þe geornor gebetan.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#IICn_4-1.lnote.oe.24"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="310" ed="#liebermann"/>We beodað, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wiðersacan ⁊ útlagan Godes ⁊ manna of earde gewítan, buton hig gebúgan ⁊ ðe geornor gebétan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="310" ed="#liebermann"/>And we beodað, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wiðersacan ⁊ utlagan Godes ⁊ manna of earde gewitan, buton hig gebugan ⁊ þe geornar betan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4.1" corresp="#wit-d-frags"><pb n="310" ed="#liebermann"/>[4, 1] And witena<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_4-1.lnote.oe.2"/> gerædnes is, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wiðersacan ⁊ utlagan Godes ⁊ manna of earde gewitan, buton hi gebugon ⁊ þe geornor gebetan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="311" ed="#liebermann"/>Precipimus etiam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_4-1.lnote.oe.11"/>, ut ƿiþersacan (apostate<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_4-1.lnote.oe.12"/>) et útlage Dei et hominum patriam exeant, nisi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_4-1.lnote.oe.13"/> (si non) resipuerint et digne peniteant.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="311" ed="#liebermann"/>[4, 1] Edicimus etiam, ut discoli et exleges Dei et hominum a patria discedant, nisi se dedant et emendent.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="4a.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="176" ed="#robertson"/>We beodað<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IICn_4-1.robnote.fn.6"/> þæt wiðersacan ⁊ útlagan Godes ⁊ manna of earde gewítan, buton hig gebúgan ⁊ ðe geornor gebétan<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#IICn_4-1.robnote.fn.9"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="256" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And we beodað þæt wiðersacan and utlagan Godes and manna of eardæ gewitan butan hig gebugan and þe geornor gebetan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="311" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wir gebieten (Beschluss der Witan ist <hi rend="italic">D</hi>), dass [kirchlich] Abtrünnige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_4-1.lnote.de.1"/> und von Kirche<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_4-1.lnote.de.2"/> und Menschen Geächtete aus dem Lande weichen, es sei denn, sie unterwerfen sich und büssen um so eifriger.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And we command (it is the decision of the witan, D) that apostates and outlaws of God and men depart from the land, unless they submit and atone all the more eagerly.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_4-1.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="177" ed="#robertson"/>We enjoin that apostates and those who are cast out from the fellowship of God<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_4-1.robnote.n.2"/> and of men shall depart from the land, unless they submit and make amends to the utmost of their ability.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="257" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And we command that apostates and those in defiance of the laws of God and the realm are to leave this land unless they submit and most sincerely repent.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="311"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_41">VIII Atr 41f.</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. VIII Atr. 41 f.</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="357"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_41">VIII Atr 41–42</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 4:1: Cn 1018 8  VIII Atr 41-42</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="357"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-016">Cn 1018 8</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 4:1: Cn 1018 8  VIII Atr 41-42</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="93"><label>=</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-016">Cn 1018 8–8.1</ref> <quote>Cn 1018 8 – 8:1 = II Cn 4:1–2</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><label>used in I–II Cnut</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-016">Cn 1018 8</ref> <quote>Kennedy’s table:  (VIII Æthelred 41) | D 8 | II Cnut 4.1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><label>used in I–II Cnut</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-017">Cn 1018 8.1–10.1</ref> <quote>Kennedy’s table: – | D 8.1–10.1 | II Cnut 4.1, II Cnut 4.2, II Cnut 6–7.1</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Quadr.'s ‘þiþersacan’ uses þ for wynn (= wiþersacan). Liebermann compares VIII Atr 41 f.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 311, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_4-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">311</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dant <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dant Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_4-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">311</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">aus K; fehlt übrigen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">from K; lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_4-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">311</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">über</hi> wi. <hi rend="italic">Dm; fehlt KRHk; davor</hi> id est <hi rend="italic">fügt zu T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">above wi. Dm; lacking in KRHk; before it T adds id est</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_4-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">311</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">n. <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> si n. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">n. K; si n. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_4-1.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">310</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">später geändert in</hi> -de <hi rend="italic">G;</hi> -de <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">later altered to -de G; -de Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_4-1.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">310</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">buton <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">buton Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_4-1.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">310</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-gon <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-gon Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_4-1.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">310</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">betan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">betan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_4-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">310</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">aus V Atr.?</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">from V Atr.?</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_4-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">202</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">dyscolus</hi> bed. in Vulg. <hi rend="italic">Petr</hi>. 1, 2, 18 ‘unbillig, unfreundlich’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">dyscolus</hi> means in the Vulg. <hi rend="italic">Petr</hi>. 1, 2, 18 ‘unfair, unkind’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_4-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">202</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> abtrünnig; Exkommunikation 1; Verbannung 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> abtrünnig; Exkommunikation 1; Verbannung 4</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_4-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">352</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. VIII Atr. 41.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_4-1.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">352</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. <hi rend="italic">utlah wið God</hi>, Procl. of 1020, cap. 17.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_4-1.robnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">176</biblScope></bibl><label>beodað</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">And witena</hi> &amp;c. D.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_4-1.robnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">176</biblScope></bibl><label>gebétan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">betan</hi> A, Ld.</seg></note>
